      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This is a preliminary report of 31 patients treated with Henning's spiral bundle nails for subcapital humeral fractures. Complications included motion restriction at the elbow joint (n = 4), elbow pain caused by pin migration (n = 2), misalignment attributable to incorrect reduction (n = 4), and redislocation attributable to improper technique (n = 1), humeral head perforation (n = 3), caudal subluxation of the humeral head (n = 3), and local infections at the insertion site (n = 1). Immobilization was 3 weeks on average. By using the scoring scheme of Constant and Murley, 11 patients showed a moderate result, whereas 19 patients had an excellent outcome."},
